# Environment variables (root reference)

Copy backend environment file before running the API:

```bash
cd backend
cp .env.example .env
```

## Backend (`backend/.env`)

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `NODE_ENV` | `development` or `production` |
| `PORT` | API port (default `5000`) |
| `DATABASE_URL` | MySQL connection string |
| `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET` | Access token secret |
| `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET` | Refresh token secret |
| `JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES_IN` | Access token expiry |
| `JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES_IN` | Refresh token expiry |
| `CORS_ORIGIN` | Frontend origin |
| `SMTP_HOST` | Mail host (optional) |
| `SMTP_PORT` | Mail port |
| `SMTP_USER` | Mail user |
| `SMTP_PASS` | Mail password |
| `UPLOAD_DIR` | Upload directory |
| `MAX_FILE_SIZE` | Max upload bytes |
| `RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS` | Rate limit window |
| `RATE_LIMIT_MAX` | Max requests per window |
| `AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX` | Auth route limit |

## Example `DATABASE_URL`

```env
DATABASE_URL="mysql://root:@localhost:3306/lead_management_crm"
```

## Frontend

Frontend uses Vite proxy to the backend in development. No secrets are required in the frontend for local dev.

**Never commit real `.env` files or production secrets.**
